# Pathology 05: solving A x = b where A is a Hilbert matrix is
# hopelessly ill-conditioned even at modest n. The exact-arithmetic
# answer is fine; the floating-point answer is junk because the
# condition number grows roughly as exp(3.5 n).

narrate "Build the n x n Hilbert matrix  H_ij = 1 / (i + j + 1)."
narrate "Pick x_true = (1, 1, ..., 1). Compute b = H x_true."
narrate "Solve H x = b. Compare x against x_true."
narrate "In exact arithmetic the recovery is exact; in double we see"
narrate "how much (condition number) * (machine epsilon) the rounding"
narrate "inflates to."

# At n=10 cond(H_n) is ~1.6e13, so the recovered x has lost most of
# its digits. Note that --interp and --exec produce slightly
# different recovered errors here -- the matrix amplifies ulp-level
# differences in intermediate arithmetic, so the two backends
# disagree on the trailing digits. That disagreement IS the
# pathology being demonstrated. The pathology smoke check excludes
# this file from strict interp/exec parity for that reason; the
# lesson text and the structure of the output are stable.
n = 10

# Build H. Indices are 0..n-1 so use H_ij = 1 / (i + j + 1).
H = zeros(n, n)
for i to n {
    for j to n {
        H[i, j] = 1.0 / (i + j + 1)
    }
}

# True solution: all-ones vector.
x_true = ones(n)

# Right-hand side b = H @ x_true.
b = H @ x_true

narrate "First three entries of b:"
b0 = at(b, 0)
b1 = at(b, 1)
b2 = at(b, 2)
show b0
show b1
show b2

# Solve.
x_solved = zeros(n)
solve(H, b, x_solved)

narrate ""
narrate "Recovered x_i (should all equal 1); errors x_i - 1:"
for i to n {
    xi = at(x_solved, i)
    err = xi - 1.0
    show i
    show xi
    show err
}

# Maximum-entry error.
max_err = 0.0
for i to n {
    e = at(x_solved, i) - 1.0
    if e < 0 { e = -e }
    if e > max_err { max_err = e }
}
narrate ""
narrate "Maximum absolute error in recovered x:"
show max_err

# ---- Lesson ------------------------------------------------------

print("")
print("Lesson: condition number measures how much input error a linear")
print("        system multiplies into output error. Hilbert matrices")
print("        are the canonical ill-conditioned family: cond(H_n) ~")
print("        exp(3.5 n). At n=8 the conditioning is ~3e10 and we've")
print("        already lost half our digits; at n=12 the conditioning")
print("        is ~1e16, every digit is noise, and even the two knot")
print("        execution backends produce visibly different answers")
print("        because the matrix amplifies ulp-level differences in")
print("        intermediate arithmetic. The 'fix' isn't a better solver")
print("        -- it's not asking the question. Reformulate so the")
print("        matrix is well conditioned (Chebyshev nodes for")
print("        polynomial fitting, orthogonal bases for least-squares,")
print("        etc.).")
